# Line endings, and why this file has to exist.
#
# The output contract is held byte for byte by goldens, and the requests behind
# it by cassettes, all under testdata/. On a Windows checkout with the default
# core.autocrlf, git rewrites text files to CRLF on the way out, jr still writes
# LF, and every golden comparison fails about a contract nobody touched. The
# tests are right and the checkout is wrong.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Every testdata/ is exempt from translation in both directions, not merely
# pinned to LF. A cassette holds the bytes a server sent and a fuzz corpus entry
# holds the bytes that broke something; whether either is text is not git's
# call.
**/testdata/** -text
